      "markdown": "The O2, Greenwich, London SE10\n\n# Oxygen Freejumping, The O2\n\nBespoke digital wallcoverings in a fine-line geometric design for Oxygen Freejumping at The O2, joined by overlap and splice so the lines run unbroken.\n\n![Oxygen Freejumping at The O2: purple-lit seating area with bespoke digital wallcoverings.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/oxygen-o2-01-800.webp)\n\n## At a glance\n\nClient, materials & project facts\n\n**Client**\n: Oxygen Freejumping\n\n**Designer**\n: –Not recorded\n\n**Main contractor**\n: –Not recorded\n\n**Maker and paper**\n: Muraspec (digital print, wide vinyl)\n\n**Area or rooms**\n: –Not recorded\n\n**Scope**\n: Installation of bespoke digital wallcoverings\n\n**Year**\n: 2018\n\nIn September 2018 we installed bespoke digital wallcoverings for Oxygen Freejumping at The O2 in Greenwich: a fine-line geometric design printed by Muraspec on wide vinyl, running along the seating areas and corridors.\n\n## At a glance\n\n- **Where:** Oxygen Freejumping, The O2, Greenwich\n- **When:** September 2018\n- **Scope:** installation of bespoke digital wallcoverings\n- **Wallcovering:** Muraspec digital print on wide vinyl\n- **Joint:** overlap and splice\n\n## Overlap and splice\n\nWide vinyl is hung with the edges overlapped, then cut through both layers at once and the offcuts removed, so the two edges meet exactly. On a design of fine white lines on a dark ground, that is the only way to keep each line continuous across the joint.\n\n## Photographs on this page\n\nOur own photographs, first posted on our Instagram, [@mrwallcover](https://www.instagram.com/mrwallcover/), on 22 September 2018 ([BoCE7LPnvqA](https://www.instagram.com/p/BoCE7LPnvqA/)).\n\n## Photographs\n\n![Close-up of a fine-line geometric wide-vinyl wallcovering, Oxygen Freejumping, The O2.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/oxygen-o2-03-800.webp)\n\n![Bespoke geometric digital wallcovering under purple lighting, Oxygen Freejumping, The O2.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/oxygen-o2-02-800.webp)\n\n![Seating zone with patterned wallcovering under coloured lights, Oxygen Freejumping, The O2.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/oxygen-o2-05-800.webp)\n\n![Fine-line geometric wallcovering hung with overlap-and-splice joints, Oxygen Freejumping, The O2.](https://www.mrwallcover.com/media/img/r/oxygen-o2-06-800.webp)\n\nHow the commission ran\n\n## The same standards, on every commission.\n\nWhether the client is a hotel group, a designer or a household, the job runs the same way. These are the parts a photograph never shows.\n\n01\n\n### Survey and scope, room by room\n\nWe measure the wall that will actually be hung, allow for the repeat and the wastage, and write a scope of works room by room before anyone orders paper.\n\n02\n\n### Preparation decides the finish\n\nWalls are filled, made good and primed until they are true. If a wall is not ready for the material specified, we say so before the last drop is ordered.\n\n03\n\n### Protection and containment\n\nFloors, furniture and finished joinery are protected as part of the hang. Work is contained and the place is left tidy each evening. In a home we are visitors; in a hotel we work around the house.\n\n04\n\n### Batch and shade control\n\nDeliveries are checked against the measure, and batches and shading are managed so that a corridor of rooms reads as one surface.\n\n05\n\n### Set out from the room's focal points\n\nPattern is set out from chimneypieces, doorcases and bed walls, so the design meets the cornice and the joinery with composure.\n\n06\n\n### One team, then the return visit\n\nThe people who start are the people who finish. Four to six weeks after completion we come back to look at every seam and edge, and the workmanship is guaranteed for twelve months.\n\n[See the finish up close: seams, internal corners, edges and joins from our own installations](https://www.mrwallcover.com/details/)\n\nBy [Dorin Burcus](https://www.mrwallcover.com/about/#dorin), founder · Last updated 11 October 2026\n",
